From: Mahalakshmi Kailasam <mahalakshmik@ami.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tiogapass: use full JPEG frames

AST2500 can return decodable JPEG payloads without an EOI marker in the
last two bytes. Do not discard those frames before sending them to the VNC
client.

Use standard full-frame JPEG capture for TiogaPass. The AST2500 driver does
not implement VIDIOC_G_SELECTION, which partial-frame mode requires for its
rectangle metadata.

Signed-off-by: Mahalakshmi Kailasam <mahalakshmik@ami.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform specific]
---
 ikvm_server.cpp     | 8 --------
 start-ipkvm.service | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ikvm_server.cpp b/ikvm_server.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/ikvm_server.cpp
+++ b/ikvm_server.cpp
@@ -209,14 +209,6 @@ void Server::sendFrame()
 
         noValidDataFrameCount = NO_VALID_FRAME_COUNT_RESET;
 
-        if (!(data[video.getFrameSize(i) - 2] == 255 &&
-              data[video.getFrameSize(i) - 1] == 217))
-        {
-            video.releaseFrames();
-            video.getFrame();
-            continue;
-        }
-
         if (calcFrameCRC)
         {
             if (frame_crc == -1)
diff --git a/start-ipkvm.service b/start-ipkvm.service
index 3333333..4444444 100644
--- a/start-ipkvm.service
+++ b/start-ipkvm.service
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ ConditionPathIsMountPoint=/sys/kernel/config
 [Service]
 Restart=always
 ExecStartPre=/usr/bin/create_usbhid.sh disconnect
-ExecStart=/usr/bin/obmc-ikvm -v /dev/video0 -k /dev/hidg0 -p /dev/hidg1 -f 15 -s 1 -m 2
+ExecStart=/usr/bin/obmc-ikvm -v /dev/video0 -k /dev/hidg0 -p /dev/hidg1 -f 30 -s 0 -m 0
 
 [Install]
 WantedBy=multi-user.target